import { url } from '../../lib/site.js';
---
<p>
  <a href={url('/molecules/')}>Molecules</a> groups the data into diatomics, triatomics and polyatomics. Pick a molecule
  to see its isotopologues. Each isotopologue has its runs, newest first, with the latest run of each MARVEL version
  marked, the run's paper, its level and transition counts, plots of its levels and spectral coverage, and links to its
  energy-levels, transitions and segment files.
</p>
<p><a href={url('/references/')}>References</a> lists the paper behind every run.</p>
<p>
  <a href={url('/api/')}>API</a> explains how to query the data directly: filtering levels by quantum numbers, paging
  through transitions, and downloading files from scripts.
</p>
<p><a href={url('/submit/')}>Submitting data</a> covers how to send a MARVEL dataset for inclusion.</p>
